Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:10:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] #1: prove the delta sync fetches only the delta
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The delta lane itself shipped in f3c0f61 (Search API) and 1b1683c
(repository_dispatch), and the full pull dropped to ~15 points in 3f9285a
(#57; measured 16 points on 2026-07-31, src/mirror.ts), but nothing
exercised syncPullDelta: it shelled out to dolt, gh and rate_limit with no
seam, so the closest test (closed-at-freshness) could only grep the source
text.

Add `DeltaIo` — sql / gh / graphqlLimit — as an optional second parameter
defaulting to the live trio (no caller changes), report `fetched` (the size
of the delta the search returned) in DeltaResult, and add
test/sync-delta.test.ts: run a first sync against an in-memory mirror,
change ONE issue on a scripted Search API, run again, and assert the
second search is bounded by the first sync's cursor, returns exactly one
issue, and issues exactly one UPDATE for that row. Also pins the
delta-search metering, reopen clearing closed_at, unknown issues being
counted not written, and the date-granularity cursor.

No behaviour change on the live path. The full pull (mirror-sync.yml) runs
every 6h, not weekly — the "weekly" wording in older comments nearby is
stale and left untouched here.

Closes #1

